Z||000000||Gokart||02-19-2000||06:03 AM||||Ok! I'm about done with my scooped GT quarter window replacements from FOCOA! Nice shiny black and I made up badges for them with the help of Rodney Dickman's wheel center stickers! Here's my question-what should I use to adhere them in place? They are twice as heavy as the originals and with the air blowing through the scoop I doubt the OEM double-sided tape will work. I'm already having nightmares of driving on the highway and seeing my scoops flying in the air 500 ft. above me! I don't plan on ever having to take them off so I think some kind of 2-part epoxy will secure them for life. Any suggestions? TIA for replys!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||02-19-2000||10:00 AM||||I used the black urethane that is used to install windshields for my quarter scoops. This stuff will hold anything together, just dont get it aanywhere that you dont want it, because it is a pain to remove.||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||02-19-2000||11:03 AM||||To remove the goop if you get it somewhere unwanted. Use diesel fuel. It wont take of paint of hurt plastic/acrylic but will cut the windshield sealant goop. I use Jet A||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gokart||02-19-2000||11:23 AM||||Thanks! Where can I get this black urethane? Do they sell it at most autoparts stores or do I have to go to a glass shop to purchase some?||||reg||14
Z||000004||Cooter||02-19-2000||05:59 PM||||Most any supply shop will have it. The good stuff is made by 3M and is called Quick Set Urethane. About $10 for the tube that you use in your caulking gun.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||02-19-2000||06:19 PM||||I picked a toothpaste size tube of the same kind of stuff at Wal-Mart $3.35||||reg||1
